Description: No-echo meeting audio input for Notion AI Meeting Notes
 Notion Recorder creates a capture-only PipeWire/PulseAudio virtual microphone
 that mixes your voice with the selected speaker output, so Notion AI Meeting
 Notes transcribes both sides of a call in a single input.
 .
 The mix is never routed back to playback, so remote meeting participants never
 hear an echo, and the system default microphone is left untouched (Google Meet,
 Zoom and Teams keep using it unchanged).
 .
 Ships a GTK4/libadwaita control app with live level meters, friendly device
 pickers and an audio-flow diagram, plus an optional mic-activity daemon that can
 auto-start and stop the mix around calls.

